<!DOCTYPE html><html lang="en"><head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1"><link rel="icon" type="image/png" href="{{ asset('favicon.png') }}"><title>Privacy Policy · Proflect</title>@vite(['resources/css/app.css','resources/js/app.js'])</head><body class="legal-body"><header class="legal-header"><x-brand light/><a href="{{ route('register') }}">Back to registration</a></header><main class="legal-content"><span class="eyebrow">PROFLECT</span><h1>Privacy Policy</h1><p class="legal-intro">This page explains the information used by the Proflect customer portal and how it supports your account, program and claims.</p><h2>Information you provide</h2><p>When you register or use the portal, we collect your name, email address, phone number, vehicle details, registration number, claim descriptions and photographs. We also keep records of your plan, payments, warranty codes and claim decisions.</p><h2>How information is used</h2><p>We use this information to create and secure your account, administer your program, process payments, review claims, provide documents and send service notifications. Claim photographs are used to assess the reported damage.</p><h2>Sharing and service providers</h2><p>Information may be shared with providers that help operate the portal, process payments, deliver email or review claims, only as needed for those services. We may also disclose information when required by law.</p><h2>Storage and security</h2><p>We use access controls and other reasonable safeguards to protect portal information. No online system can guarantee complete security. Please use a strong password and contact support if you suspect unauthorised access.</p><h2>Your choices</h2><p>You can review and update basic profile details in the portal. To ask about access, correction or deletion of information, contact support. Some records may need to be retained for program administration or legal obligations.</p><h2>Policy updates</h2><p>We may revise this policy when the service or its data practices change. The current version will be available here.</p><p class="legal-updated">Last updated: 21 September 2026</p></main></body></html>
